      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>Ensuring a seamless destination delivery experience for two-wheelers and motorcycles requires a meticulous, protocol-driven handover process. This phase is critical for validating the vehicle's integrity against its initial state and confirming legal transfer of custody. The procedure begins strictly during daylight hours to eliminate lighting ambiguities that could mask minor scratches or paint defects.</p>
<p>The driver or receiver must conduct a comprehensive visual re-inspection, systematically comparing the current condition of the bike against the high-resolution photographs captured at the pickup point. This step ensures that any pre-existing damage is documented and that no new transit-related harm has occurred, safeguarding both the carrier’s liability and the customer’s asset value.</p>

<p>Following the visual assessment, the handover process moves to mechanical and documentary verification. The receiver must verify the odometer reading on the motorcycle against the figure recorded in the Legal Metrology (LR) bilty and the original booking documentation.</p>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">This cross-check is essential to confirm that the vehicle has not been improperly used during transit and that the mileage data is consistent with the journey’s duration and distance.</p>
